Closed forms of `0 + 1 + ... + (n - 1)` for `n = arg0 & 255`, each cheaper than the last.

--- function sum
--- candidate
fn @sum(arg0: i256) -> i256 {
  bb0:
    v4 = and arg0, 255
    v0 = sub v4, 1
    v1 = mul v4, v0
    v2 = div v1, 2
    v3 = add v2, 0
    ret v3
}
